0..71 Comment "//! `buffer-moved` transfers an owned buffer to a mock ring submission."
72..75 Comment "//!"
76..155 Comment "//! The submission takes the buffer by move, not by borrow. The kernel owns the"
156..232 Comment "//! buffer until the operation completes [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]. The"
233..305 Comment "//! pathological twin refuses the old owner when it closes the buffer as"
306..327 Comment "//! `UsedAfterClose`."
328..331 Comment "//!"
332..411 Comment "//! The checker consumes the owner\'s endpoint at `send`. The mock kernel closes"
412..491 Comment "//! the buffer before it posts the completion. The buffer is a linear resident,"
492..563 Comment "//! the end of a forked owner. Its move into a submission is delegation"
564..659 Comment "//! [Honda-1998-language_primitives_type_discipline_structured_communicationbased_programming]."
660..663 Comment "//!"
664..726 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/buffer-touched.gandr"
727..770 Comment "//! - cites: [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]"
771..874 Comment "//! - cites: [Honda-1998-language_primitives_type_discipline_structured_communicationbased_programming]"
875..878 Comment "//!"
879..978 Comment "//! [boats-2020-notes_on_io_uring]: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/ \"boats, Notes on io-uring\""
979..1227 Comment "//! [Honda-1998-language_primitives_type_discipline_structured_communicationbased_programming]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0053567 \"Honda, Vasconcelos and Kubo, Language Primitives and Type Discipline for Structured Communication-Based Programming\""
1229..1268 Comment "// The ring\'s protocol and its entries."
